#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:94
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`<name>/<name>.json` with name, version, `repository` (the planned home), `livesAt` (where it sits today), `needs`, and only the directories that exist, each declared with its files in one commit. `<name>/platform.ts` from the first commit, so no climb out of the directory ever needs rerouting. Scaffolded by `init-folio --staged <path>`, which writes those two files and nothing at the host root; never `--instance`, which writes a whole repository."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:153
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`bun run cat seed:ready --layer <name> --rehearse` copies the layer and what it needs into a scratch workspace of sibling directories and runs the tests there. Run the gates rather than scanning imports: a static scan misses files the gates load at run time, and renaming the directory changes every generated page."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A content type's creation skill asked whether the new graph goes in a new repository or inside this one, and the answer was inside this one. Or a graph already staged here is to be taken through the rest of its lifecycle."
msgstr ""

