#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Create a knowledge graph inside a harnessed repository as a layer of its own, grow it there, and when it should leave, stage it for separation and move it whole into a new repository. Declared in place with a planned `repository` and a `livesAt` saying where it sits today; staged by one import seam (`<name>/platform.ts`), the separation guard and a self-contained rehearsal; then, each behind an explicit owner confirmation, the repository is created, the staged contents are copied in with their history, the declaration is re-pointed, a fresh clone is verified, and the in-repo copy is frozen in the kept trashcan. The light sibling of kg-separation, which splits a graph into a content and a tools repository; this moves a data layer whole, and shares kg-separation's seeding gateway and decision table. DRAWN IN PHASES (owner, 2026-11-08, Q-B1-3 A): it keeps its own grow-in-place and staging steps, and calls the authorise, move and cut-over phases it shares with kg-separation."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn:186
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Create the repository, drain, copy the staged contents in, re-point the declaration, verify a fresh clone, then consume, release and check every identifier dereferences."
msgstr ""

